# .beads/*.jsonl are exports of the authoritative Dolt DB (.beads/embeddeddolt).
#
# issues.jsonl is a per-record STATE file (one JSON object per issue, keyed by
# id). It was previously `merge=union`; that is correct for an append-only log
# and WRONG for state. Union concatenates hunks, so it happily keeps a stale
# "status":"open" row for an issue the DB has already closed, and never
# reconciles two rows carrying the same id. Measured 2026-08-16: main held
# claude_verilog_test-0eh and -pzj as "open" at both the #159 and #160 merge
# points, weeks after both were closed, and beads' post-merge import replayed
# those stale rows back into the DB -- silently reopening them twice. Bead b1o.
#
# The custom driver regenerates the file from the DB instead of reconciling two
# texts, so the result is correct by construction. Register it per clone with
# `make setup` (or `make setup-beads`); `make verify-tooling` checks it.
.beads/issues.jsonl        merge=beads-export

# interactions.jsonl really IS an append-only audit log, so union is right here.
.beads/interactions.jsonl  merge=union
